title: view:refresh
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Generic panel commands]]
kind: reference
summary: Read what a panel shows again (self / a panel type)

Reads what a panel shows again: the focused panel with `self`, the panel type named otherwise ([[Generic panel commands]]). What that means depends on the panel:

|!Panel |!Reads again |
|[[metarecord-list panel]] |runs its query again; the cursor stays on its metarecord when it is still listed |
|[[file-manager panel]] |the displayed directory, and what the repository says of its entries, keeping the cursor where it was. The panel does not watch the disk: a file another program created appears on a refresh |
|[[path-ref panel]] |the repository's fields and the children shown |
|[[log panel]] |the log, and the operation gone into |
|[[trash panel]], [[recent panel]], [[duplicates panel]] |the entries, the recently viewed metarecords, the groups |
|[[repos panel]] |the loaded repositories, their tasks and their tracking notices |
|[[file panel]] |the file or the folder, as it is on disk now; a medium goes back behind its poster, its position kept. Playing it from the start is <<key "file:restart" Shift+r>> |
|[[metarecord-detail panel]] |the metarecord shown; while an edit is in progress, it asks first |
|[[sync panel]] |the loaded repositories, the pair kept, then the status or the stored plan, whichever is shown — never a new plan or a run |
